<Layout title="Terms & Conditions" description="Terms for using the Ankit Jobs & Staffing India website and its candidate and recruiter forms — free registration, vacancies, selection and contact links.">
  <PageHero title="Clear Expectations. Informed Decisions." crumb="Terms & Conditions" eyebrow="Terms & conditions" text="The terms that apply when you use this website and its forms."/>
  <section class="section"><article class="container legal-content"><h2>About this website</h2><p>Ankit Jobs &amp; Staffing India is a recruitment and job placement business. This website provides career information, current openings and online forms for candidates and employers.</p><h2>Free for candidates</h2><p>Registration and recruitment support are free for candidates. Ankit Jobs &amp; Staffing India does not charge candidates a registration fee. If anyone asks you for money in our name, contact us before paying.</p><h2>Candidate and recruiter forms</h2><p>When you submit a form, you confirm that the details are accurate and that you are allowed to share them. Submitting a form, making an enquiry or registering does not guarantee a vacancy, interview, selection or employment. How we handle submitted details is explained in the <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p><h2>Vacancies and selection</h2><p>Vacancies are listed as provided by hiring companies and may change or close at any time. Employers make their own selection decisions and set the terms of employment, including salary, location and joining arrangements.</p><h2>Using contact links</h2><p>WhatsApp, telephone and email links connect you to external communication services, which have their own terms. Keep enquiries general and do not send sensitive documents through these links — use the online forms instead.</p><h2>Website content</h2><p>We try to keep information on this website accurate and up to date, but it may change without notice. Please read the <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> as well.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>Contact <a href="/contact-us/">Ankit Rai</a> to clarify anything about these terms before sharing information or agreeing to a service.</p></article></section>
</Layout>
